Plate diameter in the image is about 355 px. If it is a standard dinner plate (~26 cm), that is about 0.073 cm per px. The greens cover roughly 240 px by 250 px, or about 17 by 18 cm. They form an irregular mass that fills about 35% of the plate area and sits roughly 2-3 cm high. That gives a volume of about 250 cm³ when loosely packed, and cooked greens are airy, so I estimate about 130 g.

There are a few carrot pieces, about 15 g, and a little oil or juice sheen, about 5 g.

